{"name":"Teatime Mauve","hex":"#c8a89e","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"teatime","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The traditional time, in the late afternoon, for serving tea (the meal).","A social gathering or conversation centered on sharing gossip, rumors, or other personal news."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/teatime"},{"term":"mauve","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A rich purple synthetic dye, which faded easily, briefly popular c. 1859‒1873 and now called mauveine.","A pale purple or violet colour, like the colour of the dye after it has faded."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a pale purple colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mauve"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tea (meal)","blocks":[{"text":"Tea is an umbrella term for several different meals consisting of food sometimes accompanied by tea to drink. The English writer Isabella Beeton, whose books on home economics were widely read in the 19th century, describes meals of various kinds and provides menus for the \"old-fashioned tea\", the \"at-home tea\", the \"family tea\", and the \"high tea\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Afternoon_meal_in_Tiffin.jpg/330px-Afternoon_meal_in_Tiffin.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tea_(meal)","wikidata":"Q245009"},{"title":"Mauve","blocks":[{"text":"Mauve is a pale purple color named after the mallow flower. The first use of the word mauve as a color was in 1796–1798 according to the Oxford English Dictionary, but its use seems to have been rare before 1859. Another name for the color is mallow, with the first recorded use of mallow as a color name in English in 1611."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/32/Wilde_Malve.JPG/330px-Wilde_Malve.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mauve","wikidata":"Q604079"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Floris_Claesz._van_Dyck_001.jpg/500px-Floris_Claesz._van_Dyck_001.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Floris_Claesz._van_Dyck_001.jpg/1280px-Floris_Claesz._van_Dyck_001.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Floris_Claesz._van_Dyck_001.jpg/500px-Floris_Claesz._van_Dyck_001.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFloris_Claesz._van_Dyck_001.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/Gr%C3%BCn_-_A_Group_of_Artists.jpg/500px-Gr%C3%BCn_-_A_Group_of_Artists.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/Gr%C3%BCn_-_A_Group_of_Artists.jpg/500px-Gr%C3%BCn_-_A_Group_of_Artists.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Thé avec des artistes (\"Tea with the artists\"), Jules Grün, 1929","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGr%C3%BCn_-_A_Group_of_Artists.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/Anna_Maria%2C_Marchioness_of_Tavistock.jpg/330px-Anna_Maria%2C_Marchioness_of_Tavistock.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/Anna_Maria%2C_Marchioness_of_Tavistock.jpg/330px-Anna_Maria%2C_Marchioness_of_Tavistock.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Anna Russell, Duchess of Bedford, 1820, the founder of afternoon tea","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAnna_Maria%2C_Marchioness_of_Tavistock.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thum